WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.238
Why this matters.

2
00:00:01.238 --> 00:00:05.300
A certificate is a signed naming claim
that has already been handed out.

3
00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:07.795
It sits in device stores, on smart cards,

4
00:00:07.795 --> 00:00:12.238
in load balancers and in trust
stores nobody remembers configuring.

5
00:00:12.238 --> 00:00:14.638
It doesn't move when the directory moves.

6
00:00:14.638 --> 00:00:19.012
It keeps working until it expires,
and then whatever relied on it stops.

7
00:00:19.012 --> 00:00:23.775
Three properties make AD CS the hardest
part of Active Directory to leave.

8
00:00:23.775 --> 00:00:28.975
An enterprise CA is wired into the forest:
its templates, enrollment services,

9
00:00:28.975 --> 00:00:34.013
NTAuth trust and publication points
live in the configuration partition.

10
00:00:34.013 --> 00:00:38.884
The cloud replacements cover only
part of the estate: Cloud PKI issues

11
00:00:38.884 --> 00:00:43.588
to Intune-managed devices, and Intune
doesn't manage Windows Server.

12
00:00:43.588 --> 00:00:48.487
And domain controllers need certificates
for as long as domain controllers exist.

13
00:00:48.487 --> 00:00:52.299
Meanwhile the rules are moving
under certificates already issued.

14
00:00:52.299 --> 00:00:57.092
Public TLS maximum validity
is two hundred days today,

15
00:00:57.092 --> 00:01:03.375
a hundred days from March 15, 2027, and
forty-seven days from March 15, 2029.

16
00:01:03.375 --> 00:01:09.946
KB5014754 put domain controllers in
Full Enforcement on February 11,

17
00:01:09.946 --> 00:01:16.063
2025, and Compatibility mode has
been gone since September 9, 2025.

18
00:01:16.063 --> 00:01:23.815
NIST's draft post-quantum transition plan
proposes deprecating RSA-2048 signatures

19
00:01:23.815 --> 00:01:31.240
after 2030 and disallowing RSA and ECDSA
signatures after 2035, and OMB M-26-15 gave

20
00:01:31.240 --> 00:01:38.337
agencies a hundred and twenty days from
June 24, 2026 to submit a migration plan.

21
00:01:38.337 --> 00:01:41.638
So the move off AD CS
runs as its own program.

22
00:01:41.638 --> 00:01:43.970
It fails at expiry, not at cutover,

23
00:01:43.970 --> 00:01:47.400
which can be months later
and far from its cause.
